  "background_and_question": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1b0f78afcf23041ee638f1c8e85eb0fd65471d0468ac1cb81087694ce4b4333c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1b0f78afcf23-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Rehnquist, the petition is brought by Tom L. Carey, Warden, against Tony Eugene Saffold."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1b0f78afcf23041ee638f1c8e85eb0fd65471d0468ac1cb81087694ce4b4333c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1b0f78afcf23-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice, the Court asked what the system and time limits are for filing post\u2011conviction relief in California."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1b0f78afcf23041ee638f1c8e85eb0fd65471d0468ac1cb81087694ce4b4333c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1b0f78afcf23-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice, the Court also inquired whether, after a trial court denies relief, the only review mechanism is filing an original writ with the Court of Appeals."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1b0f78afcf23041ee638f1c8e85eb0fd65471d0468ac1cb81087694ce4b4333c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1b0f78afcf23-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 8,
              "start": 8
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice, the Court asked whether a party can begin the process in a higher court."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1b0f78afcf23041ee638f1c8e85eb0fd65471d0468ac1cb81087694ce4b4333c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1b0f78afcf23-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 14,
              "start": 14
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice, the Court queried whether filing a petition in the superior court, rather than an appeal, is the correct procedure in California."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1b0f78afcf23041ee638f1c8e85eb0fd65471d0468ac1cb81087694ce4b4333c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1b0f78afcf23-0000-0007"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 18,
              "start": 18
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice, the Court asked whether the majority of courts hold that the filing of a petition in the Court of Appeals is required."
      }
    ],
