  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Ogden",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "1b0f78afcf23041ee638f1c8e85eb0fd65471d0468ac1cb81087694ce4b4333c",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-1b0f78afcf23-0001-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 27,
                "start": 27
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Ogden, the petitioner argues that the rule adopted by unanimous courts of appeals\u2014tolling gaps between stages of the state habeas process when the next stage is initiated timely\u2014should apply to California."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Ogden",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "1b0f78afcf23041ee638f1c8e85eb0fd65471d0468ac1cb81087694ce4b4333c",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-1b0f78afcf23-0001-0005"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 28,
                "start": 28
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Ogden, the petitioner contends that California\u2019s system of original writs should be subject to the tolling rule for the entire period, for two reasons, including the text of the statute."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Ogden",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "1b0f78afcf23041ee638f1c8e85eb0fd65471d0468ac1cb81087694ce4b4333c",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-1b0f78afcf23-0002-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 38,
                "start": 38
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Ogden, the petitioner cites the O\u2019Sullivan case, applied by the Ninth Circuit in James v. Giles, requiring filing and submission of claims to the California Supreme Court to fully exhaust state remedies."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "1b0f78afcf23041ee638f1c8e85eb0fd65471d0468ac1cb81087694ce4b4333c",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-1b0f78afcf23-0003-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 53,
                "start": 53
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The petitioner argues that the \u201cgap theory\u201d should not apply in California because the state gives unequal rights to the two sides, creating a functional appeal that should be treated differently for federal purposes."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "1b0f78afcf23041ee638f1c8e85eb0fd65471d0468ac1cb81087694ce4b4333c",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-1b0f78afcf23-0003-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 54,
                "start": 54
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, the petitioner notes that Congress was concerned about undue delay and wrote into AEDPA that the time a state post\u2011conviction application is pending shall not count toward the federal limitation period."
        }
      ],
